# 3D Ellipsoid Model

To model an ellipsoid shape with specific dimensions in a 3D modeling package like Blender, Maya, or Autodesk 3ds Max, you can follow these general steps:

Create a New Project:
Start a new project or open an existing one in your chosen 3D modeling software.

Add a 3D Shape:
Most 3D modeling software provides various ways to create basic shapes. You can typically start with a simple geometric shape like a cube or sphere, and then modify it to achieve the desired "thick pancake" shape.

Scale the Shape:
Use the scaling tool to adjust the dimensions of the shape to match your desired values. In your case, set the dimensions along the x, y, and z axes to represent your "thick pancake."

Modify the Shape:
To create a flattened ellipsoid or other distortions you may need to use more advanced modeling tools. You can typically use deformation tools or modifiers that allow you to change the shape. These tools might include options for scaling along specific axes or bending the shape.

Smooth the Surface:
Depending on the software, you may need to smooth the surface of your shape to make it look more like desired shape. You can use subdivision surfaces or smoothing modifiers for this purpose.

Texturing and Materials:
Apply textures and materials to your model to give it the desired appearance. You can create a texture for your  shape.

Lighting and Rendering:
Set up lighting in your scene to properly illuminate your model. Then, render your 3D scene to create a final image or animation.

The specific steps may vary depending on the 3D modeling software you are using, so it's important to refer to the documentation or tutorials for your software of choice. The key is to scale and modify a basic shape to achieve the dimensions and appearance of your shape as described.
